      "writtenOn": "2021-11-18T12:51:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason we have this mechanism for binder proxies is mainly because having many binder proxies makes the binder kernel driver quite a bit slower (for lookup), and this is in the critical path of a binder call. For stubs this is less of an issue, because once you know the proxy, it\u0027s a O(1) operation to get the stub.\n\nWe\u0027ve also found that the proxy limit mechanism is quite error-prone; for example, it\u0027s really hard to take into account the effect of the garbage collector.\n\nThat is also something I worry about with this change; what if there are a significant amount of Pending Intents stuck waiting to be GCd?",
      "parentUuid": "5f4aa703_016cdc00",
